<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sa'id al-Dawla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1002</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sa'id al-Dawla was the last effective Hamdanid emir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a>, reigning from 991 to 1002. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> was squeezed between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> and the Fatimid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a>, and he relied on Byzantine help against Fatimid sieges. Real power lay with his chamberlain Lu'lu', who probably had him poisoned and soon ended Hamdanid rule.</p></div>
